        },
        {
          "id": "q4",
          "type": "short",
          "objective": "O4",
          "key": "The code, not the model, owns the control flow and fixes a single search; the fix is to let the model decide whether and what to search next, in a loop with a stopping limit, so that part becomes an agent.",
          "answers": {
            "claude-sonnet-5-5": "The code fixes a single search so the model cannot react to the results; letting the model run an agent loop that can issue further searches with different terms fixes it",
            "claude-haiku-5-5": "The design hard-codes a single search, so the model cannot choose a follow-up query based on what it reads; the fix is to let the model run a loop that issues further searches with new terms until it has enough information"
          },
          "match": {
            "claude-sonnet-5-5": null,
            "claude-haiku-5-5": null
          },
          "solvers_agree": null
        },
        {
